  <prompt>
    Populate the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (schema from task 003; ADR from task 004) at the point every `sprk_communication` message is persisted — both **outbound send** (`CommunicationService.cs` persist ~lines 689-727) and **inbound capture** (the ingestor/normalizer persist). For each persisted message, write **one junction row per (message × person/address × role)** where role ∈ {`From`, `To`, `Cc`, `Bcc`}:

    - `sprk_communication` → the message (required, message-grain parent).
    - Resolved person → **exactly one** of `sprk_systemuser` / `sprk_contact` set, `sprk_isresolved=true`, `sprk_addresstext` retained as provenance. Resolve email→person by REUSING `ParticipantCorrelationRung`'s email→contact resolution (`QueryContactByEmailAsync`) — do NOT add a second resolver.
    - Unresolved external address (owner Q-D) → row with **both** person lookups null, `sprk_isresolved=false`, `sprk_addresstext` = the raw email, so `participant=` (task 051) still surfaces the external party and it is back-fillable when a contact is later created.
    - `sprk_role` = the choice integer for {From,To,Cc,Bcc} (from task 003 schema); `sprk_name` = `"{personDisplay|address} — {role}"`.

    **The junction write is best-effort / non-fatal (mirror R1 enrichment discipline): a junction-write failure MUST NOT fail the send or drop the captured message** — the `sprk_communication` record is the source of truth; participant rows are a derived index. **The write must be idempotent per message** — re-processing the same message (e.g. inbound echo/retry) MUST NOT duplicate rows.

    This is a WRITE on the shared persist path. Characterization-test the existing email + messaging send/capture flows and keep them green BEFORE extending. `parallel-safe:false`. `/conflict-check` before the PR.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication subsystem. Authority on the shared `Services/Communication/` persist path (`CommunicationService.cs` send + the inbound capture persist), the `Engine/Rungs/ParticipantCorrelationRung.cs` email→person resolution, and `Models/ParticipantReference.cs`. Fluent in ADR-034 (person-identity tuple intent → the R2 path-C 2-typed-lookup form), ADR-028 (impersonation / no `new` credential), ADR-032 (Null-Object kill-switch + symmetric registration for any feature-gated write), the best-effort/non-fatal enrichment discipline (R1 NFR-02), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Every persisted `sprk_communication` message — outbound send and inbound capture — emits `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction rows at message grain: one row per (message × person/address × role {From,To,Cc,Bcc}), resolved persons carrying exactly one typed lookup (`sprk_systemuser` XOR `sprk_contact`) + `sprk_isresolved=true`, unresolved external addresses carrying `sprk_isresolved=false` + `sprk_addresstext` (Q-D). Email→person resolution reuses `ParticipantCorrelationRung` (`QueryContactByEmailAsync`) — no second resolver. The write is best-effort/non-fatal (never fails the send or drops a captured message) and idempotent per message (no duplicate rows on re-processing). Existing email/messaging send + capture flows stay green (characterization tests). Build clean; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R1/email-r4 store participants as `;`-separated TEXT (`sprk_from`/`sprk_to`/`sprk_cc`) on `sprk_communication` — not queryable by person or role. `ParticipantCorrelationRung.cs` resolves email→contact→memberships at capture time but persists nothing queryable (investigation §5). Task 003 adds the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (message-grain parent lookup + `sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact` typed nullable lookups + `sprk_role` choice {From,To,Cc,Bcc} + `sprk_addresstext` + `sprk_isresolved`); task 004 authors its schema ADR (ADR-034 path-C tension). THIS task is the write side: populate those rows at the persist point so FR-02's `participant=` facet (task 051) has an exact, role-precise, FK-backed index — replacing the wrong-results text-LIKE fallback.

      Component Justification (§11): (1) Existing — `ParticipantCorrelationRung.QueryContactByEmailAsync` already resolves email→person; `CommunicationService` already persists the message; `ThreadMembershipDerivationService` answers record→people, NOT person→communications (investigation §5). No queryable person→communications structure exists. (2) Extension — this task adds NO new service and NO new resolver: it reuses the existing resolution and writes rows into the task-003 junction at the existing persist point. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete, spec-cited): without the junction the `participant=` filter is impossible, person filter degrades to text-LIKE (wrong results, no role precision), and external parties are invisible/unfilterable — named FR-02/FR-08 contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      Best-effort discipline (mirror R1 NFR-02): the `sprk_communication` record is the source of truth; junction rows are a derived index. A junction-write exception is logged/deferred and MUST NOT fail an outbound send or drop an inbound-captured message. Idempotency: re-processing the same message (inbound echo/retry per the R1 echo-dedup seam) MUST NOT create duplicate rows — key the write on (communication × person/address × role).

      Shared-path discipline (root §10 F.3): this edits `CommunicationService.cs` (outbound persist ~lines 689-727) and the inbound capture persist — the same shared `Services/Communication/` surface as 070 and the frozen email/messaging flows. Characterization-test the existing flows and keep them green BEFORE extending; `parallel-safe:false`; hand-trace + reproduce before trusting the wiring.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs (outbound persist ~lines 689-727 — write junction rows after the message persists; inbound capture persist path)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/ParticipantCorrelationRung.cs (REUSE `QueryContactByEmailAsync` email→person resolution; do NOT fork)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/ParticipantReference.cs (reuse the resolved-person reference shape)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Access/CommunicationAccessFilter.cs (context — the read-side filter task 051 applies over these rows)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ (CommunicationModule DI — symmetric/unconditional registration for any new writer service, ADR-032)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (characterization tests for existing send/capture + new junction-write tests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-08">One junction row per (message × person/address × role {From,To,Cc,Bcc}) at MESSAGE grain (parent = `sprk_communication` lookup; owner Q-A — no thread-grain rows). Resolved person = exactly one of `sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact` set + `sprk_isresolved=true`. Populated at BOTH capture and send.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08 / Q-D">Unresolved external address writes a row: both person lookups null, `sprk_isresolved=false`, `sprk_addresstext` = raw email. `participant=` MUST still surface it; it is back-fillable when a contact is later created. MUST NOT silently skip external parties.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034 (path-C, spec §ADR Tensions)">Person identity uses the two typed nullable lookups (`sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact`, exactly one set for a resolved person) — honoring ADR-034's intent (typed identity, no text-name matching, no polymorphic parent). MUST NOT reintroduce fuzzy text-name matching or a Guid+type text tuple. Reuse `ParticipantCorrelationRung` resolution; add no second resolver.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02 discipline (R1)">The junction write is best-effort / non-fatal: a write failure is logged/deferred and MUST NOT fail an outbound send or drop an inbound-captured message. The `sprk_communication` record remains the source of truth.</constraint>
    <constraint source="idempotency">Re-processing the same message (inbound echo/retry) MUST NOT duplicate rows — key the write on (communication × person/address × role).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Writes go through the canonical impersonation/Dataverse interfaces; MUST NOT `new` a credential / `ConfidentialClientApplication`; inject central `TokenCredential` + canonical Dataverse interfaces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 / ADR-018">If the junction write is feature-gated, use the Null-Object kill-switch with SYMMETRIC/unconditional registration — no asymmetric `if (flag)` registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Shared `Services/Communication/` edit — characterization-test existing email/messaging send + capture flows and keep them green BEFORE extending (F.3 empirical-reproduction-first). `parallel-safe:false`; never concurrent with 070. `/conflict-check` before the PR. bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline (expected ≈0, no new package); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §11">State the concrete FR-02/FR-08 failure modes prevented (no `participant=`, text-LIKE wrong results, invisible external parties). No new resolver, no new access mechanism, no new package.</constraint>
  </constraints>

