  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `CommunicationService.cs` (outbound persist ~lines 689-727 + the inbound capture persist), `ParticipantCorrelationRung.QueryContactByEmailAsync`, `Models/ParticipantReference.cs`, the task-003 junction schema, and the task-004 ADR. Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + §11. Map the exact persist points (outbound + inbound) where the message id is known.</step>
    <step order="2">CHARACTERIZATION FIRST (root §10 F.3): write/confirm characterization tests over the existing email + messaging send AND inbound-capture persist flows; run them green BEFORE any edit. These are the regression guard for the shared-path change.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the junction-write logic: after a message persists, enumerate the From/To/Cc/Bcc addresses; for each, reuse `ParticipantCorrelationRung` resolution (`QueryContactByEmailAsync`) → resolved (exactly one of `sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact` + `sprk_isresolved=true` + `sprk_addresstext` provenance) or unresolved (both null + `sprk_isresolved=false` + `sprk_addresstext`). Write one row per (message × person/address × role) with `sprk_role` = the task-003 choice integer and `sprk_name` = `"{personDisplay|address} — {role}"`.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the write at BOTH persist points (outbound send + inbound capture) so `participant=` is complete regardless of direction (spec: "populated at capture/send").</step>
    <step order="5">Make the write best-effort/non-fatal (mirror R1 enrichment): wrap so a junction-write exception is logged/deferred and does NOT fail the send or drop the captured message.</step>
    <step order="6">Make the write idempotent per message: key on (communication × person/address × role) so re-processing (inbound echo/retry) does not duplicate rows.</step>
    <step order="7">If the write is feature-gated, register via ADR-032 Null-Object with symmetric/unconditional registration (no asymmetric `if (flag)`); otherwise register unconditionally. Confirm ADR-028 (no `new` credential; canonical interfaces).</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests: (a) send with resolved To + Cc → rows with the correct typed lookup (`sprk_systemuser` XOR `sprk_contact`) + role + `isresolved=true`; (b) UNRESOLVED external To → row with both lookups null, `isresolved=false`, `addresstext` set (Q-D); (c) inbound capture writes rows on the capture path too; (d) BEST-EFFORT: a junction-write exception does NOT fail the send / does NOT drop the captured message (message still persisted); (e) IDEMPOTENT: re-processing the same message yields NO duplicate rows; (f) NEGATIVE: no row ever sets BOTH `sprk_systemuser` and `sprk_contact`; (g) characterization: existing send/capture flows still green.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm the characterization tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline (expected ≈0 — no new package).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: best-effort/non-fatal, idempotency-no-duplicates, resolved XOR unresolved invariant, reuse-not-fork of the resolver, symmetric registration); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-08, ADR-034 path-C, ADR-028, ADR-032, §10/§11). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; shared `Services/Communication/` persist path; MUST NOT overlap with 070 or other BFF writers; coordinate merge-order).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (050 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (where the write hooks on each persist path, the idempotency key, the feature-gate/registration choice).</step>
  </steps>

